Hosted bsdtar pair proposal, 2026-10-15. SOURCE AUTHORED ONLY.

No current app/test file or Archive experimental bundle was edited. No local
bootstrap, original binary, test, build, syntax checker or patch checker ran.
The proposed helper and two narrow patches have not been applied or accepted.

Committed-source candidate authored separately:
products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs

It permits only standard GitHub-hosted Windows, CI=true, GITHUB_ACTIONS=true,
Node24.16.0, and an explicit owned RUNNER_TEMP evidence child. It fetches the
two stable official Microsoft Symbol Server URLs, caps each transfer at its
exact recorded size with a45-second deadline, requires SHA256 and PE identity,
and retains images only under ignored .local/bsdtar-original. Initial/terminal
receipts distinguish acquisition from actual original execution. It does not
launch originals, inspect signatures via a native program or claim a test pass.

EXE: tar.exe,92280 bytes, SHA256
4e598a8cec84af779e3377442fce2b94b976f614ed4c6e5a665e19308fd1e379
https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols/tar.exe/BE8EDDEC14000/tar.exe

DLL: archiveint.dll,1482752 bytes, SHA256
ca36efd61b33586e4cee69513bf3dcc8d20b65f37bd6495d5d82eb15833b5824
https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols/archiveint.dll/0B7F5A2E16a000/archiveint.dll

These exact reference images remain in the local WinSxS build26100.9278
components. Source investigation read their version metadata, static import
strings and PE headers and performed one targeted hash per identified image.
HEAD-only requests returned200 with the exact expected lengths. Actual hosted
GET digest validation remains pending; no remote image was downloaded locally.
Ephemeral redirected SAS URLs must not be saved or used as permanent sources.

The old historical receipt pinned only tar.exe. A second retained3.8.8 DLL
from build26100.9549 has a different hash; therefore this newly explicit
paired-build9278 DLL identity is not proof of which DLL the old run loaded.
Preserve every historical receipt/test snapshot and label new results as a
new oracle-dependency epoch. Do not weaken the EXE pin or any skip/fail gate.

Why a WINDIR-only adapter is insufficient: current tests copy the EXE into a
private fixture directory before invoking it. The EXE imports archiveint.dll.
Without copying the pinned DLL beside that executed copy, Windows may resolve
the current system DLL. The proposed helper authenticates both cache files
first, writes both with exclusive creation in the existing owned temporary
fixture, rechecks copies and preserves the existing EXE basename expected by
test bodies. The patches change only the import and local oracle-loader body;
test bodies, original banners, frozen fixtures and expected outcomes remain.

Hosted validation sequence, AFTER a reviewed new derivative epoch composes
the work-only helper/patches and records exact before/after identities:

node products/rea-studio/scripts/bootstrap-cloud-bsdtar.mjs --evidence <unique absolute RUNNER_TEMP child>

Then use the streaming cloud collector or an equivalent recorded hosted
selection to run formats.test.mjs and zstd.test.mjs with the complete pinned
7-Zip prerequisites also acquired. Both loaders execute --version from the
paired private copy before comparisons, retaining the existing banner checks.
Record actual process exits/output, before/after source identities, the new
paired DLL identity and the bootstrap receipt. A separate small hosted
smoke invocation may run `.local/bsdtar-original/tar.exe --version` after
both images authenticate; it is actual original execution and must be counted
separately from acquisition and comparison calls. No binary upload or system
file replacement is required.

Microsoft primary reference for timestamp/image-size symbol-store indexing:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/debug/using-symstore
Fallback package identified by Microsoft Support/Catalog is KB5120998,
build26100.9278 (2026-08-27), approximately5GB for x64. Official small-image
retrieval avoids that bulk download; it does not alter Microsoft licensing.
